# gitattributes-example — force GitHub to classify .boru files as BORU.
#
# Drop these lines into a file named `.gitattributes` at the ROOT of your
# repository (create it if it does not exist), commit, and push. GitHub's
# Linguist reads `.gitattributes` per-repo, so this takes effect even
# before BORU is merged into github/linguist upstream — it is the local
# fallback while the upstream PR is in flight, and a permanent override if
# you want to be explicit.
#
# `linguist-language=BORU` overrides detection and forces every matching
# path to be reported as BORU in the repository language bar and rendered
# with the BORU grammar (once linguist ships one). The name on the right
# MUST match the language key added to linguist's languages.yml ("BORU").

*.boru linguist-language=BORU

# --- optional extras -------------------------------------------------------
#
# Mark generated / vendored .boru fixtures so they do NOT count toward the
# repo's language stats (and are collapsed in diffs). Adjust the globs to
# your layout; these are examples, not required.
#
# testdata/**/*.boru linguist-generated=true
# vendor/**/*.boru   linguist-vendored=true
#
# Treat a docs/example directory as documentation rather than code, so it
# is excluded from the language bar:
#
# examples/**/*.boru linguist-documentation=true
